<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albert Frederick, Duke of Prussia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1553–1618</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Albert Frederick (1553–1618) was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> from 1568, the son and successor of Albert, the first duke. Mentally ill from his youth, he was unable to rule, and his Hohenzollern relatives of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-ansbach">Brandenburg-Ansbach</a> and then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> governed as regents. On his death the duchy passed to his son-in-law, Elector <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-sigismund-elector-of-brandenburg">John Sigismund</a>, creating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-prussia">Brandenburg-Prussia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albert-frederick-duke-of-prussia.jpg" alt="Albert Frederick, Duke of Prussia" width="320" height="367" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Albert_Frederick,_Duke_of_Prussia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
